_ do emit-chained-assign
    - id SyntaxId
    - op Operator
    - lhs SyntaxId
    - rhs SyntaxId

` An assignment to a place that is a link of an optional chain. The value is evaluated,
` whatever the chain holds, and then the chain up to the place, in TypeScript's order for `=`,
` which an assigning operator, whose place TypeScript reads first, follows here too. Where each
` optional it tests holds a value, the value is converted and stored as it is in a place
` written with no chain, by an assigning operator what it gives for the place and the value,
` and where one holds nothing, nothing is stored.
. object = receiver-of(lhs)
if object == 0
    refuse(.refused-statement, id)
    =
. made = emit-expression(rhs)
. value = apart(made, rhs, true)
. given = made.type
if is-unmade(lhs)
    emit-unmade(lhs)
    =
. skipped = ir.reserve-block()
. held = held-receiver(lhs, object, skipped)
. pin-mark = pins.length
pin(object, held.operand, held.type)
pin(rhs, value, given)
emit-assign(id, op, lhs, rhs)
unpin(pin-mark)
jump(skipped)
ir.start-block(skipped)

────────────────────
_ do emit-forward-set
    - id SyntaxId
    - op Operator
    - lhs SyntaxId
    - object SyntaxId
    - rhs SyntaxId

` An assignment to a member of a union that each case answers with its own setter, as the
` type pass planned it. The value is evaluated, and then the union, once each. Both are given
` to the function made for the member where a case may panic, and else each case is set in
